# Token Efficiency

Canonical source: `/Users/macbook/Github/vibeCodingRules/token-efficiency.md`

## The Rule

Optimize for **fewer tokens**, not for less work. Correctness, exploration, and implementation quality are non-negotiable.

## Responses

- Bullets only — what changed, why, how to verify.
- No filler, recap of the prompt, or step-by-step narration of actions already taken.
- No restating file contents the user can open.
- Use line-range citations only when they aid a decision.
- Ask only when blocked or a choice is required.

## Code

- Smallest correct diff — prefer surgical edits.
- Align every file you open/edit with applicable rules; fix violations in scope; no repo-wide drive-by renames.
- No verbose narrating comments. WHY only.
- Match existing conventions; reuse helpers instead of duplicating.

## Tool use

- Targeted exploration; do not re-read unchanged files.
- Parallelize independent reads/greps/searches.
- Do not skip exploration when behavior or edge cases are unclear.
- Run the project's formatter/linter on touched files; never bulk-reformat for style-only churn.

## What NOT to cut

- Investigation required for correctness
- Tests, types, and error handling when required
- Commit/PR messages when requested — complete sentences, no padding
